<title>INDIA: INDIAN CRUDE, PETROLEUM OUTPUT IMPROVE IN MAY.</title>
<headline>INDIAN CRUDE, PETROLEUM OUTPUT IMPROVE IN MAY.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's crude petroleum production grew to 2.87 million tonnes in May from 2.80 million in the same month last year, the government said in a monthly report on the economy on Monday.</p>
<p>    PETROLEUM OUTPUT     May 97    May 96	  Apr-May</p>
<p>							  1997/98  1996/97</p>
<p>    Crude		    2,873     2,800    5,679     5,556</p>
<p>    Petroleum Products   5,569     5,217    10,785   10,341</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in thousands of tonnes and preliminary. Figures for petroleum products relate to throughput.</p>
</text>
